t, we define ${a}_{n}=(-1)^{n+1}{4}^{n}{x}^{n+3}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{4}^{n+1}{x}^{n+4}}{(-1)^{n}{4}^{n}{x}^{n+3}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|-4x| \\\\  & =4|x|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ In this case, the convergence condition is satisfied if \n\n$$\n4|x|<1\\,⇒\\,|x|<\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the radius of convergence is $R=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-82846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "72ee4476-9ccd-5e3a-a1aa-efe576b4d55e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82851/selection/bcb3a13c00508924772cd99f87896054b10639a22a6eee40c385ea4e630fbe24" :answer/id #uuid "7524908c-1af1-57de-a616-9752e4e6f425" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82851/selection/4da4aa62a241ae37bf130d02d4c1f95f4b28eb04f4e8dd44d6a50c09d8d3999d" :answer/id #uuid "57a4fd65-a20d-55cc-b2e0-b7862f3b7fba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82851/selection/c655b6f86977e4b14c5c1fcb656a1bbd12a39077e0b70924c843d6eed4f6f437" :answer/id #uuid "6b1754f9-8896-55c8-a39f-35bd6b97c2fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82851/selection/c5ca126c80e62a84b72d00d27a1145a341622a3566772ce4f4b8d929e1e0ca34" :answer/id #uuid "13a8bd8a-64c9-5b42-b68c-7a0c6e7831d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82851/selection/93dbe47a86ec74fec47617cbf7dcc1164d2d445805c60b96c25576c117d6bf35" :answer/id #uuid "f8c970d9-9ddd-5b3e-b38f-594d2c4d6370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer